{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 19,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.091,
            0.539,
            0.12
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "What you have learnt"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.133,
            0.894,
            0.167
          ],
          "content": "n **Carbon is a versatile element that forms the basis for all living organisms and many of the things we use.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.17,
            0.894,
            0.203
          ],
          "content": "n **This large variety of compounds is formed by carbon because of its tetravalency and the property of catenation that it exhibits.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.206,
            0.893,
            0.239
          ],
          "content": "n **Covalent bonds are formed by the sharing of electrons between two atoms so that both can achieve a completely filled outermost shell.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.241,
            0.892,
            0.276
          ],
          "content": "n **Carbon forms covalent bonds with itself and other elements such as hydrogen, oxygen, sulphur, nitrogen and chlorine.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.278,
            0.894,
            0.327
          ],
          "content": "n **Carbon also forms compounds containing double and triple bonds between carbon atoms. These carbon chains may be in the form of straight chains, branched chains or rings.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.329,
            0.894,
            0.364
          ],
          "content": "The ability of carbon to form chains gives rise to a homologous series of compounds **in which the same functional group is attached to carbon chains of different lengths.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.365,
            0.893,
            0.4
          ],
          "content": "The functional groups such as alcohols, aldehydes, ketones and carboxylic acids **bestow characteristic properties to the carbon compounds that contain them.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.401,
            0.774,
            0.419
          ],
          "content": "n **Carbon and its compounds are some of our major sources of fuels.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.421,
            0.892,
            0.439
          ],
          "content": "n **Ethanol and ethanoic acid are carbon compounds of importance in our daily lives.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.441,
            0.894,
            0.491
          ],
          "content": "The action of soaps and detergents is based on the presence of both hydrophobic **and hydrophilic groups in the molecule and this helps to emulsify the oily dirt and hence its removal.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.447,
            0.97,
            0.552,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.517,
            0.614,
            0.547
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "E X E R C I S E S"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.563,
            0.582,
            0.582
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "1. Ethane, with the molecular formula C H has"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.583,
            0.39,
            0.601
          ],
          "content": "**(a) 6 covalent bonds.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.604,
            0.391,
            0.622
          ],
          "content": "**(b) 7 covalent bonds.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.623,
            0.392,
            0.641
          ],
          "content": "**(c) 8 covalent bonds.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.643,
            0.39,
            0.661
          ],
          "content": "**(d) 9 covalent bonds.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.663,
            0.751,
            0.682
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "2. Butanone is a four-carbon compound with the functional group"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.683,
            0.374,
            0.701
          ],
          "content": "**(a) carboxylic acid.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.703,
            0.32,
            0.721
          ],
          "content": "**(b) aldehyde.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.723,
            0.301,
            0.741
          ],
          "content": "**(c) ketone.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.742,
            0.303,
            0.76
          ],
          "content": "**(d) alcohol.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.761,
            0.894,
            0.795
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "3. While cooking, if the bottom of the vessel is getting blackened on the outside, it means that"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.798,
            0.531,
            0.817
          ],
          "content": "**(a) the food is not cooked completely.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.818,
            0.533,
            0.837
          ],
          "content": "**(b) the fuel is not burning completely.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.838,
            0.36,
            0.856
          ],
          "content": "**(c) the fuel is wet.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.857,
            0.499,
            0.877
          ],
          "content": "**(d) the fuel is burning completely.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.1,
            0.916,
            0.304,
            0.93
          ],
          "content": "Carbon and its Compounds"
